Usage: ruralz dev run [DIR] [FLAGS]

Local ruralzd with Hot Reload.

Renders DIR for --env, or from the process environment, into a private
directory and runs a local ruralzd on that test render, bound to loopback,
with a generated operator token. Once ruralzd is ready the command prints
its Revision, admin URL, listeners and a ruralz dev tap command line, then
polls DIR, the --environments and --secret-overrides files and the files
these name, and swaps in a new test render once a change has settled;
ruralzd Hot Reloads it. Ctrl-C stops ruralzd through a Drain, and a second
Ctrl-C ends the Drain at once.

Arguments:
  DIR  Bundle directory or one-file Bundle (default .)

Flags:
  --env NAME                Render with this Environment's overlay and variables, read from --environments
  --environments FILE       Local Environment resources
  --ephemeral-ports         Rewrite every listener port and admin.port to a free loopback port
  --help                    Print this help
  --memory-state-store      Replace the Gateway's stateStore with driver memory
  --output text|json        Output format (text or json, default text)
  --ready-timeout DURATION  How long to wait for /readyz after the launch and for each activation (default 30s)
  --ruralzd PATH            The ruralzd to launch (default: beside ruralz, else on PATH)
  --secret-overrides FILE   Local files replacing secretRefs: provider:name keys, file path values
